  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A handover pad can record unresolved maintenance, low supplies, and promised follow-ups; outgoing and incoming stewards have a brief overlap.\", \"decision\": \"How should unfinished studio duties pass between stewards?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe incoming steward inspects the handover pad and relevant studio areas, then asks the outgoing steward about unclear duties. Questions arise from an initial independent check, concentrating the overlap on information that is actually missing.\nBoth stewards make a brief circuit of the studio and record unresolved duties together on the handover pad. The record is built from shared observations, so the incoming steward sees the conditions behind each follow-up.\nThe outgoing steward writes unresolved duties on the handover pad and walks through them with the incoming steward. The written record guides a short conversation before responsibility passes to the next person."
    }
  ],
